--
sv-benchmarks pthread-memsafety/list1.c (expected false, valid-deref). Many
properties (pointer, allocation and leak checks) and a violation that needs 3
rounds, so the search solves the same formula several times. The first
version re-added the goal disjunction as a clause at every round; the
converter returned its cached gate variable, which Glucose's simplifier had
eliminated during the previous solve, and the run aborted in
SimpSolver::addClause_ right after round 1. Both questions are now asked by
frozen assumptions only. The calibration table has 1 round for this task,
which is why it was answered SUCCESSFUL there.
